  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to the urgent needs of people affected by the war and empowering local actors in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine is now three years into Russia&apos;s full-scale invasion. Increasingly complex and multifaceted humanitarian needs continue to persist nationwide, but especially amongst displaced populations, evacuees and populations in the southern and eastern regions near the frontline. This Action aims to address the most pressing, immediate humanitarian needs of the most vulnerable war-affected populations in Ukraine whilst simultaneously building local capacities. IOM is doing this through a coordinated, multi-sectoral response focused on shelter and non-food items (NFI), and camp coordination and camp management (CCCM). This Action also addresses cross-cutting issues to strengthen the capacity and knowledge of IOM and its partners, ensuring the delivery of evidence-based assistance is safe, dignified, and well-coordinated. The Action targets areas in South and East Ukraine as well as other areas heavily affected, including in North-East Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
